---
import H from "@/components/H.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="FRC 12148"
    description="Team V.A.N. is a student-led FIRST Robotics Competition team in Palm Bay, Florida, building career-ready STEM and leadership skills across Brevard and Indian River counties."
>
    <H class="mb-4">Team V.A.N.</H>

    <p>
        Student-led FIRST Robotics Competition (FRC) Team building career-ready
        skills through hands-on STEM and sports-like rigor.
    </p>

    <Section>
        <H level="h2">What we do</H>
        <p>
            Founded in 2026, Team V.A.N. is a rookie FRC team dedicated to
            giving students hands-on experience in engineering, problem-solving,
            and most importantly, decision-making and leadership.
        </p>
        <p>
            As a rookie team, having ample support for our first official
            competition season is crucial, as we have to build our entire
            operational infrastructure and technical foundation from the ground
            up.
        </p>
        <p>
            Our goal is to let students control and manage every aspect of the
            team, from sponsorships, fundraising, and community outreach to all
            critical design decisions and technical implementations of the
            robot.
        </p>
        <p>
            On our team, students learn how to design, build, and program
            industrial-size robots while developing vital business, marketing,
            and presentation skills to prepare for future leadership
            opportunities.
        </p>
        <p>
            With our main build space in Palm Bay, we are near Palm Bay Magnet,
            Bayside High, and Heritage High in Brevard County. We are also the
            closest FRC team to Sebastian River High, Vero Beach High, and
            Indian River Charter High in Indian River County.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Our Mission & Community Impact</H>
        <p>
            Our region encompasses several Title 1 schools and historically
            underserved neighborhoods where access to specialized STEM programs
            is severely limited. We are committed to lowering barriers to entry
            so that local students across Brevard and Indian River counties,
            regardless of financial background, have a direct pathway to
            real-world engineering and technology experience.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Sponsorship & Partnership</H>
        <p>
            Partnering with local businesses directly empowers our students to
            gain career-ready skills and technical mastery. As a community
            sponsor, your support helps us lower cost barriers and cover
            operating expenses. In return, sponsors are featured prominently on
            our official team T-shirts and website.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Join us</H>
        <p>
            We are always looking for passionate prospective students to join
            our growing team. Whether you're interested in the engineering or
            business side of things, you would make an impact! No matter your
            experience level.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Want to be a mentor?</H>
        <p>
            Experienced individuals in the area who want to guide and support
            our students are encouraged to reach out. If you have expertise in
            mechanics, electronics, business, or any other relevant field, we
            would love to have you on board as a mentor.
            <br />
            Shoot us an email at{" "}
            <a
                href="mailto:contact@teamvan.org"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                contact@teamvan.org
            </a>
            .
        </p>
    </Section>
</Layout>
